// - The record is the carrier. The asker takes one ('pool.take(ask)', from any
//   thread: the pointer to a record holding ask and an OpCore with nothing in
//   it) and fills its request: 'kind' (diag.kindRecv, ...), 'handle', 'buf',
//   'bytes' or 'bufs' (Options: None is nothing here; 'bufs', a Uni[Chain],
//   makes a kindSend a gather, as SendChain is), 'at', 'deadline' (forever()
//   for none; a timer's own time for diag.kindTimer), 'group', 'lane' and
//   'work' for a Call, 'setPeer(addr)' for SendTo and Connect. Only its
//   address crosses to the loop's thread; 'qnext' is the asker's link for
//   queueing it there.
