//   An early record is not let go: the kernel and the loop still hold it.
// - A loop that dies dissolves every asker's record it still holds into its
//   pool, after cancelling and draining it: the record's asker part dies
//   there, so an answer it owed is abandoned. Records the asker holds (taken
//   and not started, or handed back by takeDone) are the asker's. A record
//   away with its job (THE BLOCKING POOL) is its job's: it is dissolved, its
//   answer abandoned, when it comes home.
